-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Federal wave F6 — eleven contested standalone House rolls, ingested and mapped
-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Generated by scripts/vr-gen-federal-wave-f6-migration.mjs from
-- db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f6.json and db/vr-federal-wave-f6-vote-seed.json. Do not
-- hand-edit; regenerate.
--
-- WHAT THIS WAVE ADMITS: eleven measures, eleven passage roll calls, 1284
-- attributed member votes and 11 issue mappings on 4 keys that were already
-- live and already poled — climate_action, energy_production, lands_energy,
-- permitting_reform. No new issue key. No floor moved. No promote, no
-- retraction, no weight or polarity change to any existing row.
--
-- WHY IT IS AN INGEST WAVE AND NOT A MAPPING WAVE. F5 proved that a
-- mapping-only census over this corpus converts nothing: both measures it
-- surfaced as unmapped gaps had already been refused by name. So F6 queried
-- the refusal record FIRST and applied it as a pre-filter, and it caught 54 of
-- the 178 contested rolls before a single text was read. The 124 survivors are
-- votes this corpus has never held.
--
-- THE ATTRIBUTION FINDING, which is what actually moves anyone. The eight thin
-- House files each held exactly two acts, both on the same pair of
-- Congressional Review Act resolutions, ten short of the member floor of 12.
-- The cause was attribution, not vocabulary: none of the eight was in
-- db/vr-member-map.json, so every one of the 645 House rolls of the 119th was
-- unattributable to them. Eight SEED_SLUGS entries and a
-- federal_wave_f6_aug2026 roster wave fixed that, and the member floor counts
-- MAPPED records — stance-helpers.js:1112 reads memberRecordCount,
-- voting-record.js:2266 passes _pdxRecordMappedCounts(pid).votes, and that
-- helper skips a record with no issue row — which is why this wave ingests and
-- maps in one pass. All eight are recorded with a side on all eleven rolls: 2
-- + 11 = 13 against a floor of 12.
--
-- WHAT IT REFUSES, IN WRITING, and the seed carries the full argument for
-- each: four measures on the runbook's study-and-report rule (H.R. 3015, H.R.
-- 3638, H.R. 3109, H.R. 3617), one on the standing appropriations refusal
-- (H.R. 4553), one as out of subject scope (H.R. 1834, whose title says
-- gridlock and whose text extends a health-coverage subsidy), nine District of
-- Columbia measures for want of a key, and 22 individual issue keys across the
-- eleven admitted measures. The three refusals on the study-and-report rule
-- cost this wave three acts and put the eight thin members one below the
-- floor; the slice was re-sized by reading more text, not by softening a
-- refusal.
--
-- THE NEW-KEY DECISION: refused. A District of Columbia key passes the
-- recurrence test (nine contested measures) and fails vocab rule 5 — the nine
-- subjects are immigration enforcement, policing, the criminal code,
-- sanitation, judicial nominations, cash bail and juvenile transfer, and the
-- only thing they share is the jurisdiction they act on. The District is the
-- venue, not the subject. No key added, so issue-scope.js and
-- alignment-tool.js are byte-identical to HEAD, no SHELL_ASSETS file changed,
-- and CACHE_VERSION stays where it is: data-only SQL does not bump it.
--
-- THE MEASURED READ EFFECT, because a densification wave has to publish its
-- own cost. Projected with node scripts/vr-federal-fpi.mjs --set all --waves
-- f1,f2,f3,f4,f5,f6 --drift over all 343 federal members: the thin band goes
-- empty 0 · thin 10 · readable 333 to empty 0 · thin 2 · readable 341, issue
-- rows 20400 → 20416, and 62 members' shapes move. ZERO rows stop being
-- characterised — checked on the row model's own read flag over every pid,
-- never on shape counters (runbook rule 36) — and 16 start. What DOES change
-- direction is 10 rows: they move from a one-directional tier to Split, nine
-- of them on permitting_reform, because the member's pre-existing yea on H.R.
-- 3746's NEPA title now sits beside four nays on this wave's permitting bills.
-- Nothing went dark and no floor was moved to hide it; the ten are named
-- individually in db/vr-federal-mapping-seed-f6.json under
-- readDisclosure.measuredEffect.theTenRowsThatChangedDIRECTION.
--
-- WALLS REAFFIRMED: public_schools remains a funding-level chip and H.R. 1069 stays
--   unmapped; gov_regulation is the regulatory question and was refused five more times
--   here under runbook rule 3, twice on measures whose own captions say 'regulatory';
--   no_pole keys still do not characterise, so states_federal_power was refused on
--   H.R. 3628; and no `*_balance` key was used to park anything.
-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

